    "created_at": "2022-10-28T09:05:57Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-10-28T09:05:57Z",
    "body": "Unless you take steps to copy an origin, you'll reference it, so any modifications to it should be reflected. This is what happens for instance with an `about:blank` `<iframe>`. It'll have a reference to the origin of its parent document and setting `document.domain` in either document will affect both documents as they share an origin.\r\n\r\nAs such I think this should be doable, including incrementally where we keep document's origin around, but we definitely want to be careful.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
